This project is the sibling of pptx2svg (https://github.com/uvrt/pptx2svg), also MIT
licensed, and shares its methods and several of its conventions.

The licence below covers this project's own source, tests and tooling, including the
documents under tests/fixtures/ that are generated by the scripts in tools/ -- those are
ours outright.

It does not cover the third-party documents in two directories, which are not ours and
were not generated here; each keeps its own terms, recorded verbatim in the directory's
PROVENANCE.md:

  tests/fixtures/samplelib/  from samplelib.com ("do whatever you want with the files")
  tests/fixtures/wordto/     from word.to ("free to download and use for any purpose")

Both grant use without attribution; the provenance notes are kept anyway.
tests/fixtures/filesamples/ holds only a note: the documents it describes carry no
licence and are not in this repository.

The hyphenation patterns and word lists under src/docx2svg/patterns/ are third-party data
under their own permissive licences, which src/docx2svg/patterns/SOURCES.txt reproduces.

It does not cover, and this repository does not contain, any font file. Microsoft's
typefaces -- Calibri, Cambria, Aptos and the rest -- are licensed to Office and are not
ours to redistribute in any form, including as a subset, a converted file, or an
embedded blob inside a test artefact. Measurements taken from them are facts and are
recorded here as numbers; the files they were measured from stay on the machine that
measured them. The same applies to PDFs exported by Microsoft Word: those carry embedded
font subsets, which is why the ground-truth exports live outside this tree.

